Chapter: UsbCamFrame
  cites Works chapter GopXhci
  cites Works chapter GopUsbCam
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 Control, bulk and interrupt each carry bytes in this tree and each
 have a test. Isochronous had neither: no TRB type, no endpoint type,
 no frame read, in either xHCI driver. codex-vm has presented a UVC
 camera on root port 3 the whole time, delivering a colour-bar test
 pattern over isochronous transfers that nothing ever asked for. The
 port argument here is the zero-based PORTSC index, which the slot
 context turns into the one-based root port number, so the camera on
 root port 3 is reached as index 2.

 What each line proves. `open` says the streaming interface was found
 at the alternate setting that HAS an endpoint: alt 0 declares none,
 so a walk that took the first matching interface would configure a
 camera that can never stream, and `dci=5` is endpoint 2 IN, the
 isochronous one. `read=0` is the completion actually arriving.
 The pixels are the payload: the pattern is eight vertical colour bars
 twenty pixels wide, luma alternating 16 and 235 by bar, so reading
 x=0, x=20 and x=40 samples three consecutive bars and pins both the
 content and the stride. A frame of zeroes -- a buffer nobody wrote --
 fails every one of them.

Section: Test

  probe : XhciHost, UsbDev, Integer -> Text
  probe (xh) (dev) (cfg) =
    let total = usb-cfg-total cfg 255
    in let iface = cam-find-stream-iface cfg 0 total
    in if iface < 0 then "open: no streaming interface"
    else let cam = cam-open xh dev cfg iface total
    in if cam.uc-ok == False then "open: failed"
    else let r = cam-read-frame cam
    in "open: ok=1 dci=" & show (cam.uc-dci) & " alt=" & show (peek-byte cfg (iface + 3))
      & "\nread=" & show r
      & "\nluma: " & show (cam-luma cam 0 0) & " " & show (cam-luma cam 20 0) & " " & show (cam-luma cam 40 0)
      & "\nchroma: " & show (cam-chroma cam 0 0) & " " & show (cam-chroma cam 20 0) & " " & show (cam-chroma cam 40 0)
      & "\nrow1: " & show (cam-luma cam 0 1) & " " & show (cam-luma cam 20 1)

  opening : [Console, Device.Port, Device.Mmio] Nothing = act
    xh <- xhci-connect
    if xh.xh-ok == False then print-line-uni "no host"
    else act
      let speed = xhci-reset-port xh 2
      in let dev = xhci-open-device xh 2 speed
      in if dev.ud-ok == False then print-line-uni "no device on port index 2"
      else let cfg = alloc-zeroed 256 64
      in let g = usb-get-descriptor xh dev 2 0 cfg 255
      in if g == False then print-line-uni "no config descriptor"
      else print-line-uni (probe xh dev cfg)
    end
  end
